## CSS

1. Do not animate left, right, width and other CSS properties

- Such properties cause CLS(layout shifts) and as a result Pagespped becomes worse. Safe properties for animations are: translate, rotate, opacity and other which doesn’t cause layout re-render.


2. Avoid Deep Nesting in CSS Selectors

- Consider creating new classes to reduce nesting depth. It improves maintainability, reduces specificity conflicts, and potentially improves browser performance by simplifying the DOM lookup process.

```scss
// Bad
.root {
  div {
    h2 {
    }
  }
}
// Good
.root {}
.container {}
.title {}
```
